-- e3d-io write-path gate, read back by E3D itself in a TTY session (read-only: no
-- SAVEWORK, no QUIT ? the l3_suite driver's wrapper owns the session). Rendered by
-- tools/e3d/write_gate.ps1 from this template: D:/e3dio-regression/20261007-133329-46342331/write/logs and the refnos come from the
-- e3d-write apply runs (tools/e3d/write_gate_ops/*.json) on the project copy.
--
-- Sessions e3d-write appended:
--   BOX 24384/26507 under the first ZONE 24384/47
--   GPWL 16192/2 under the WORL, GROU 16192/3 with reference members ZONE + BOX
--   EQUI 24384/26508 and EQUI 24384/26509: DESC / DESP / UUIDIA as hunks (types 22/21/20),
--     one chain across a page boundary
--   FIXING 24384/26510: ROKEYS inline type 19, ROVALS as a type-23 hunk
--   BOX A 24384/26511, B 24384/26512, C 24384/26513 under the second ZONE 24384/2498, A and B
--     referenced by the GROU; then A moved under the third ZONE 24384/22400 (move_to), C
--     put before B (reorder), B taken out of the GROU (remove_reference_member) - T1a
--   ZONE 24384/26514 with 8 200 BOXes: member count saturated at 0x3FFF (plan 1.3 #11)
--   EQUI 24384/34715 and FIXING 24384/34716: every value typed as text and set by
--     attribute name (Transaction::set) under E3D's dictionary - T1b
--   BOX 24384/26507 renamed in Chinese, ZONE 24384/47 described in Chinese, the session
--     commented in Chinese ? text stored the way the header's FORMAT says (S5)
--
-- One ALPHA LOG block per question: a block's log is written only at ALPHA LOG END, so an
-- unhandled error loses that block's log and no other. Every navigation and every risky Q
-- is followed by handle any.

ALPHA LOG "D:/e3dio-regression/20261007-133329-46342331/write/logs/00_project.log" OVER
$P GATE-00-BEGIN
Q PROJ
Q MDB
$P GATE-00-END
ALPHA LOG END

